language 0.1.0
module core
  means
    Roots of the value hierarchy and their minimal refinements.

value number : thing
  means
    number: a quantity that can be compared and ordered.

value integer : number
  means
    integer: a number without a fractional part. Its sign is unrestricted.

value decimal : number
  means
    decimal: a number written in decimal notation, with fractions of ten
    represented exactly.

value text : thing
  means
    text: a sequence of characters, compared character by character and not
    decomposed into parts.

value boolean : thing
  means
    boolean: one of exactly two values, true or false.

value binary : thing
  means
    binary: a sequence of bytes carrying no character encoding.

value moment : thing
  means
    moment: a point on a time scale, ordered with respect to other moments and
    not summable with them.
